Subject: [PATCH] wined3d device reset and buffer views

Upstream commits

wined3d: Remove cached Vulkan graphics pipelines when destroying shader modules.
  Ali Milhim <alimilhim5@gmail.com>
  https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/fd6168770c0f2637a1a8a1624704094bd3e04261
wined3d: Don't add buffer views to the buffer object users list when buffer textures are unsupported.
  Doug Logan <10822557+securityvoid@users.noreply.github.com>
  https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/a0eb3b8e532dd8c3cc8a5fe34dffbd3c7bed9aa1
wined3d: Mark the buffer location valid after clearing a buffer UAV.
  Doug Logan <10822557+securityvoid@users.noreply.github.com>
  https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/7b6affa3bcec0d0c2a818485e466fc5672ef7302
wined3d: Don't tear down 3D state on device reset.
  Ali Milhim <alimilhim5@gmail.com>
  https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/837eaae305222b6158b145373602820bcda1a256
d3d9/tests: Test using shaders after a device reset.
  Ali Milhim <alimilhim5@gmail.com>
  https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/commit/a197662bbb7d7ca99f2154fd5cc0b3db86c3b3b7

The upstream regression is registered in the corresponding local test runner.

